                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.13189"} arXiv:2405.13189
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                M.S. Lukashov, Yu.A. Simonov,
                %em New ideas in nonperturbative QCD – I
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.05584"}> arXiv:2406.05584
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                J.L. Alonso, C. Bouthelier-Madre, J. Clemente-Gallardo, D. Martínez-Crespo:
                %em An axion-like mechanism for confinement in QCD
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.01047"}> arXiv:2211.01047
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Gerrit Schierholz:
                %em Renormalization Group Approach to Confinement
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.10658"}> arXiv:2509.10658
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %h4#ViaMonopoleCondensation Via monopole condensation
          %p
            An original suggestion that confinement in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            may be understood via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monopole"} monopole
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensate"} condensation
            as a dual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Meissner+effect"} Meissner effect
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#Hooft75
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gerard+%27t+Hooft"}> Gerard 't Hooft
                , in Proceed.of the Europ.Phys.Soc. 1975, ed.by A.Zichichi (Editrice Compositori, Bologna, 1976), p.1225.
            %li#Mandelstam76
              %p S. Mandelstam, Phys.Rep. 23C (1976) 145;
          %p
            (That this is indeed the case has not yet been demonstarted for plain Yang-Mills theory, but it was later shown for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N%3D2+D%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} N=2 D=4 super Yang-Mills theory
            in (
            %a{:href => "#SeibergWitten94"}> Seiberg-Witten 94
            ). What this does or does not imply for the case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            is discussed in (
            %a{:href => "#Yung00"}> Yung 00
            ) ).
          %p
            The relation to
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD+instantons"} QCD instantons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monopole"} monopoles
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD+vacuum"} QCD vacuum
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#SchaeferShuryak96
              T. Schaefer,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Shuryak"} Edward Shuryak
              = succeed "," do
                %em Instantons in QCD
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/9610451"} arXiv:hep-ph/9610451
          %p
            and analogously (at
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thermal+field+theory"} positive temperature
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calorons"} calorons
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#Greensite11"} Greensite 11, section 8.5
            %li
              %p
                P. Gerhold, E.-M. Ilgenfritz, M. Müller-Preussker,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    An
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi SU
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
                    KvBLL caloron gas model and confinement
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0607315"} arXiv:hep-ph/0607315
            %li#LarsenShuryak14
              %p
                Rasmus Larsen,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Shuryak"} Edward Shuryak
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Classical interactions of the instanton-dyons with antidyons
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 950
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1408.6563"} arXiv:1408.6563
            %li#LarsenShuryak15
              %p
                Rasmus Larsen,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Shuryak"} Edward Shuryak
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Interacting Ensemble of the Instanton-dyons and Deconfinement Phase Transition in the SU(2) Gauge Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1504.03341"} arXiv:1504.03341
          %p Further developments:
          %ul
            %li
              %em Dimensional Transmutation by Monopole Condensation in QCD
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1206.6936"}> arXiv:1206.6936
              )
          %p Discussion of confinement via an interacting field vacuum
          %ul
            %li#Rafelski90
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Johann+Rafelski"}> Johann Rafelski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Vacuum structure – An Essay
              = succeed "," do
                %em Vacuum Structure in Intense Fields
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://books.google.de/books?id=5uXcBwAAQBAJ&pg=PA14&lpg=PA14&dq=confinement+%22interacting+vacuum%22&source=bl&ots=xPGYJ-JOc-&sig=AoYbqWQeNRMg6hMSRZjJ3nzq8B0&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwjIgK68-tnYAhVCESwKHThMDykQ6AEIKTAA#v=onepage&q=confinement%20%22interacting%20vacuum%22&f=false"} GBooks
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li#Simonov18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuri+A.+Simonov"}> Yuri A. Simonov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Field Correlator Method for the confinement in QCD
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.08946"} arXiv:1804.08946
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.99.056012"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.99.056012
          %h3#ReferencesInSuperInsulators In super-insulators
          %p
            An experimentally accessible analog of confinement is observed in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superinsulators"} superinsulators
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quark"} quark
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
            is played by
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cooper+pairs"} Cooper pairs
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M.+Cristina+Diamantini"}> M. Cristina Diamantini
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlo+A.+Trugenberger"} Carlo A. Trugenberger
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Confinement and Asymptotic Freedom with Cooper pairs
                %strong 1
                77 (2018) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1807.01984"}> arXiv:1807.01984
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1038/s42005-018-0073-9"} doi:10.1038/s42005-018-0073-9
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M.+Cristina+Diamantini"}> M. Cristina Diamantini
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlo+A.+Trugenberger"} Carlo A. Trugenberger
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Superinsulators: a toy realization of QCD in condensed matter
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Roman Jackiw – 80th Birthday Festschrift
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.12541"} arXiv:2008.12541
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlo+A.+Trugenberger"}> Carlo A. Trugenberger
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Superinsulators, Bose Metals and High-
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi T
                            %mi c
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_c
                    Superconductors: The Quantum Physics of Emergent Magnetic Monopoles
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/12688"} arXiv:10.1142/12688
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlo+A.+Trugenberger"}> Carlo A. Trugenberger
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Superinsulation: Magnetic Monopoles and Electric Confinement in Condensed Matter
                %a{:href => "CQTS##TrugenbergerFeb2025"} talk at
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CQTS"} CQTS
                (Feb 2025) &amp;lbrack;slides:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Trugenberger-CQTSFeb2025.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sebastian+De+Haro"}> Sebastian De Haro
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeremy+Butterfield"} Jeremy Butterfield
              %p
                %em> The Philosophy and Physics of Duality
                , Cambridge University Press (2025) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.01616"}> arXiv:2508.01616
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://global.oup.com/academic/product/the-philosophy-and-physics-of-duality-9780198846338"} ISBN:9780198846338
          %h3#ReferencesInSuperYangMillsTheory In super-Yang-Mills theory
          %p
            Confinement in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N%3D2+D%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} N=2 D=4 super Yang-Mills theory
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+QCD"} super QCD
            by a version of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+monopole"} monopole
            condensation &amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#Hooft75"}> ‘t Hooft 75
            ,
            = succeed "&rbrack;" do
              %a{:href => "#Mandelstam76"} Mandelstam 76
          %ul
            %li#SeibergWitten94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathan+Seiberg"}> Nathan Seiberg
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Monopole Condensation, And Confinement In N=2 Supersymmetric Yang-Mills Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9407087"} arXiv:hep-th/9407087
            %li#SeibergWitten94b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathan+Seiberg"}> Nathan Seiberg
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Monopoles, Duality and Chiral Symmetry Breaking in N=2 Supersymmetric QCD
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9408099"} arXiv:hep-th/9408099
          %p Reviews with discussion of the impact on confinement in plain YM:
          %ul
            %li#Yung00
              %p
                Alexei Yung,
                %em What Do We Learn about Confinement from the Seiberg-Witten Theory
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0005088"}> arXiv:hep-th/0005088
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Dine"}> Michael Dine
                ,
                %em On the Possibility of Demonstrating Confinement in Non-Supersymmetric Theories by Deforming Confining Supersymmetric Theories
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.17134"}> arXiv:2211.17134
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Dine"}> Michael Dine
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Larkin Award Colloquium
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/k34YTIBWMNk"} YT
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Michele Della Morte, Benjamin Jäger, Francesco Sannino, Justus Tobias Tsang, Felix P. G. Ziegler,
              %em The spectrum of QCD with one flavour: A Window for Supersymmetric Dynamics
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.10514"}> arXiv:2302.10514
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %div
            %h3#PolyakovGaugeStringDualityReferences Polyakov gauge/string duality
            %p
              Key ideas underlying what is now known as
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+correspondence"} holographic
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} duality in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
              and specifically as
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-QCD+correspondence"} holographic QCD
              (see notably also at
              = succeed ")" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+light+front+QCD"} holographic light front QCD
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"} Alexander Polyakov
              (cf. historical remarks in
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#Polyakov08"} Polyakov (2008)
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge%2Fstring+duality"} gauge/string duality
              (cf. historical review in
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "#Polyakov08"} Polyakov (2008)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confined
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              (the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass+gap+problem"} mass gap problem
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} color
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+tubes"} flux tubes
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+lines"}> Wilson lines
              ) between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
              as dynamical
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strings"} strings
            %p
              Early suggestion that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confined
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              is described by regarding the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} color
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+tubes"} flux tubes
              as
              = succeed "-like" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string"} string
            %ul
              %li#KogutSusskind74
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Kogut"}> John Kogut
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonard+Susskind"} Leonard Susskind
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Vacuum polarization and the absence of free quarks in four dimensions
                  %strong 9
                  (1974) 3501-3512 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.9.3501"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.9.3501
                  ]
              %li#Wilson74
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kenneth+G.+Wilson"}> Kenneth G. Wilson
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Confinement of quarks
                  %strong 10
                  (1974) 2445 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.10.2445"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.10.2445
                  ]
                %blockquote
                  %p
                    (argument in
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+gauge+theory"} lattice gauge theory
              %li#KogutSusskind75
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Kogut"}> John Kogut
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonard+Susskind"} Leonard Susskind
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Hamiltonian formulation of Wilson’s lattice gauge theories
                  %strong 11
                  (1975) 395 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.11.395"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.11.395
                  ]
                %blockquote
                  %p “The gauge-invariant configuration space consists of a collection of strings with quarks at their ends. The strings are lines of non-Abelian electric flux. In the strong coupling limit the dynamics is best described in terms of these strings. Quark confinement is a result of the inability to break a string without producing a pair. […]”
                  %p “The confining mechanism is the appearance of one dimensional electric flux tubes which must link separated quarks. The appropriate description of the strongly coupled limit consists of a theory of interacting, propagating strings. […]”
                  %p “This picture of the strongly coupled Yang-Mills theory in terms of a collection of stringlike flux lines is the central result of our analysis. It should be compared with the phenomenological use of stringlike degrees of freedom which has been widely used in describing hadrons.”
              %li#Polyakov79
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"}> Alexander Polyakov
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em String representations and hidden symmetries for gauge fields
                  %strong 82
                  2 (1979) 247-250 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(79)90747-0"}> doi:10.1016/0370-2693(79)90747-0
                  ]
              %li#Polyakov80
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"}> Alexander Polyakov
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Gauge fields as rings of glue
                  %strong 164
                  (1980) 171-188 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(80)90507-6"}> doi:10.1016/0550-3213(80)90507-6
                  ]
                %blockquote
                  %p
                    “The basic idea is that gauge fields can be considered as chiral fields, defined on the space of all possible contours (the
                    = succeed ")." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+loop+space"} loop space
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+strings"} closed strings
                    should play the role of elementary excitations.”
              %li#MakeenkoMigdal81
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuri+Makeenko"}> Yuri Makeenko
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+A.+Migdal"} Alexander A. Migdal
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Quantum chromodynamics as dynamics of loops
                  %strong 188
                  2 (1981) 269-316 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(81)90258-3"}> doi:10.1016/0550-3213(81)90258-3
                  ]
                %blockquote
                  %p
                    “So the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/world+sheet"} world sheet
                    of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string"} string
                    should be interpreted as the color magnetic dipole sheet. The string itself should be interpreted as the electric
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+tube"} flux tube
                    in the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monopole"} monopole
                    plasma.”
              %li#Polyakov87
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"}> Alexander Polyakov
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Gauge Fields and Strings
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1201/9780203755082"} doi:10.1201/9780203755082
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/50871"} oapen:20.500.12657/50871
            %blockquote
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                = succeed "]:" do
                  %a{:href => "https://phy.princeton.edu/people/alexander-polyakov"} old personal page
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quark"} quark
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
                = succeed "\u201C,which" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+tube"} lines of force
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
                to the Coulomb law at small distances and would give permanent
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
                of quarks at large distances.”
            %p Cf. also
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  M. Lüscher:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Symmetry-breaking aspects of the roughening transition in gauge theories
                  %strong 180
                  2 (1981) 317-329 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(81)90423-5"}> doi:10.1016/0550-3213(81)90423-5
                  ]
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexei+Morozov"}> Alexei Morozov
                  , p. 6 of:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em String theory: what is it?
                  %strong 35
                  (1992) 671-714 [
                  %a{:href => "https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.1070/PU1992v035n08ABEH002255"}> doi:10.1070/PU1992v035n08ABEH002255
                  ]
            %p
              Early suggestion, due to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Liouville+theory"} Liouville field
              seen in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+string"} bosonic string
              via the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Polyakov+action"} Polyakov action
            %ul
              %li#Polyakov81
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"}> Alexander Polyakov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum geometry of bosonic strings
                %strong 103
                (1981) 207-210 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(81)90743-7"}> doi:10.1016/0370-2693(81)90743-7
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "http://qft.itp.ac.ru/polyakov-2.pdf"} pdf
            %p
              that such
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+tubes"} flux tubes
              regarded as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confining
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strings"} strings
              are to be thought of a probing higher dimensional spacetime, exhibiting a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holographic principle
              in which actual spacetime appears as a
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+brane+model"} brane
            %ul
              %li#Polyakov98
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"}> Alexander Polyakov
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em String Theory and Quark Confinement
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/conferences/970718"} Strings’97
                  %strong 68
                  (1998) 1-8 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0920-5632(98)00135-2"}> doi:10.1016/S0920-5632(98)00135-2
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9711002"} arXiv:hep-th/9711002
                %blockquote
                  %p
                    “In other words the open string flies in the
                    = succeed "-space" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,\phi)
                    = succeed ".\u201D" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mo =
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\phi=0)
              %li#Polyakov99
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"}> Alexander Polyakov
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em The wall of the cave
                  %strong 14
                  (1999) 645-658
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9809057"} arXiv:hep-th/9809057
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0217751X99000324"} doi:10.1142/S0217751X99000324
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
                %blockquote
                  %p
                    “We add new arguments that the Yang-Mills theories must be described by the non-critical strings in the five dimensional curved space. The physical meaning of the fifth dimension is that of the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} renormalization
                    scale represented by the
                    = succeed ".\u201D" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Liouville+field"} Liouville field
            %p
              eventually culminating in the formulation of the dictionary for the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+correspondence"} AdS-CFT correspondence
            %ul
              %li#GubserKlebanovPolyakov98
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steven+Gubser"}> Steven Gubser
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Klebanov"} Igor Klebanov
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"} Alexander Polyakov
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Gauge theory correlators from non-critical string theory
                %strong 428
                105-114 (1998) [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0370-2693(98)00377-3"}> doi:10.1016/S0370-2693(98)00377-3
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9802109"} hep-th/9802109
            %blockquote
              %p “Relations between gauge fields and strings present an old, fascinating and unanswered question. The full answer to this question is of great importance for theoretical physics. It will provide us with a theory of quark confinement by explaining the dynamics of color-electric fluxes.”
            %ul
              %li#PolyakovRychkov00
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"}> Alexander Polyakov
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vyacheslav+Rychkov"} Vyacheslav Rychkov
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Gauge fields-strings duality and the loop equation
                %strong 581
                (2000) 116-134 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0550-3213(00)00183-8"}> doi:10.1016/S0550-3213(00)00183-8
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0002106"} arXiv:hep-th/0002106
            %p
              and the suggestion of finding the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-QCD+correspondence"} string-QCD correspondence
            %ul
              %li#Polyakov02
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"}> Alexander Polyakov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Gauge Fields and Space-Time
                %strong 17
                S1 (2002) 119-136 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0217751X02013071"}> doi:10.1142/S0217751X02013071
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0110196"} arXiv:hep-th/0110196
            %blockquote
              %p
                “in the strong coupling limit of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+gauge+theory"} lattice gauge theory
                the elementary excitations are represented by
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+strings"} closed strings
                formed by the color-electric fluxes. In the presence of quarks these strings open up and end on the quarks, thus guaranteeing quark confinement. Moreover, in the
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SU
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(N)
                gauge theory the strings interaction is weak at large
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+tubes"} flux lines
                (strings) and not fields, thus returning us from Maxwell to Faraday. In other words it is natural to expect an exact duality between gauge fields and strings. The challenge is to build a precise theory on the string side of this duality.”
            %p Historical reminiscences:
            %ul
              %li#Polyakov05
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"}> Alexander Polyakov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Confinement and Liberation
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gerardus+%E2%80%99t+Hooft"} Gerardus ’t Hooft
                (ed.)
                %em 50 Years of Yang-Mills Theory
                (2005) 311-329 [
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0407209"}> arXiv:hep-th/0407209
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9789812567147_0013"} doi:10.1142/9789812567147_0013
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/5601"} doi:10.1142/5601
            %blockquote
              %p
                “Already in 1974, in his
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "large+N+limit#tHooft74"}
                    famous large
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi N
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
                    paper
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+tube"} flux lines
            %ul
              %li#Polyakov07
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+M.+Polyakov"}> Alexander M. Polyakov
                  , §1 in:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Beyond Space-Time
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em The Quantum Structure of Space and Time
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0602011"} arXiv:hep-th/0602011
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "http://www.solvayinstitutes.be/pdf/Proceedings_Physics/23rd_Solvay_Physics.pdf"} pdf
              %li#Polyakov08
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+M.+Polyakov"}> Alexander M. Polyakov
                  ,
                  %em From Quarks to Strings
                  [
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0812.0183"}> arXiv:0812.0183
                  ]
                %p
                  published as
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Quarks, strings and beyond
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paolo+Di+Vecchia"} Paolo Di Vecchia
                  et al. (ed.),
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em The Birth of String Theory
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511977725.048"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511977725.048
                %blockquote
                  %p
                    “By the end of ’77 it was clear to me that I needed a new strategy
                    = succeed "for" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
                    and I became convinced that the way to go was the
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge%2Fstring+duality"} gauge/string duality
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Liouville+field"} Liouville mode
                  %p
                    “I kept thinking about
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge%2Fstring+duality"} gauge/strings dualities
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Liouville+field"} Liouville mode
                    was discovered it became clear to many people including myself that its natural interpretation is that random surfaces in 4d are described by the strings flying in 5d with the Liouville field playing the role of the fifth dimension. The precise meaning of this statement is that the wave function of the general string state depends on the four center of mass coordinates and also on the fifth, the Liouville one. In the case of minimal models this extra dimension is related to the matrix eigenvalues and the resulting space is flat.”
                  %p “Since this 5d space must contain the flat 4d subspace in which the gauge theory resides, the natural ansatz for the metric is just the Friedman universe with a certain warp factor. This factor must be determined from the conditions of conformal symmetry on the world sheet. Its dependence on the Liouville mode must be related to the renormalization group flow. As a result we arrive at a fascinating picture – our 4d world is a projection of a more fundamental 5d string theory. […]”
                  %p
                    “At this point I was certain that I have found the right language for the
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge%2Fstring+duality"} gauge/string duality
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a{:href => "#Polyakov98"} Polyakov 1998
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9702076"} Klebanov 1997
                    in which he related
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D3+branes"} D3 branes
                    described by the supersymmetric Yang Mills theory to the same object described by supergravity. Unfortunately I wrongly thought that the paper is related to matrix theory and I was skeptical about this subject. As a result I have missed this paper which would provide me with a nice special case of my program. This special case was presented little later in full generality by Juan Maldacena (
                    %a{:href => "AdS-CFT+correspondence#Maldacena97a"}> Maldacena 1997
                    ) and his work opened the flood gates.”
            %p A detailed monograph:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N.+D.+Hari+Dass"}> N. D. Hari Dass
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Strings to Strings – Yang-Mills Flux Tubes, QCD Strings and Effective String Theories
                  = succeed "," do
                    %strong 1018
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-35358-1"} doi:10.1007/978-3-031-35358-1
                %p Ch. 23:
                %p
                  %em Effective String Theories (EST) of Yang-Mills Flux Tubes
                  [
                  %a{:hraf => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-35358-1_22"}> doi:10.1007/978-3-031-35358-1_22
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.10629"} arXiv:2312.10629
            %p
              Discussion of corrections of
              = succeed "-dynamics" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+tube"} flux tube
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nambu-Goto+action"} Nambu-Goto action
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  Michele Caselle, Nicodemo Magnoli, Alessandro Nada, Marco Panero, Dario Panfalone, Lorenzo Verzichelli:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Confining strings in three-dimensional gauge theories beyond the Nambu–Gotō approximation
                  %strong 2024
                  198 (2024) [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP08(2024)198"}> doi:10.1007/JHEP08(2024)198
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.10678"} arXiv:2407.10678
              %li
                %p
                  Michele Caselle, Nicodemo Magnoli, Alessandro Nada, Marco Panero, Dario Panfalone, Lorenzo Verzichelli:
                  %em
                    Effective String Theory of three-dimensional
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi SU
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi N
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(N)
                    gauge theories beyond the Nambu–Gotō approximation
                  [
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.14204"}> arXiv:2412.14204
                  ]
          %h3#confinement_via_adsqcd_correspondence Confinement via AdS/QCD correspondence
          %p
            %a{:href => "#PolyakovGaugeStringDualityReferences"} Polyakov’s ideas
            were eventually picked up by discussion of confinement in the
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-QCD+correspondence"} AdS-QCD correspondence
          %ul
            %li#Witten98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Anti-de Sitter Space, Thermal Phase Transition, And Confinement In Gauge Theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9803131"} arXiv:hep-th/9803131
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Berman"}> David Berman
                , Maulik K. Parikh,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Confinement and the AdS/CFT Correspondence
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0002031"} arXiv:hep-th/0002031
            %li
              %p
                Henrique Boschi Filho,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em AdS/QCD and confinement
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.if.ufrj.br/~boschi/pesquisa/seminarios/AdS_QCD_Confinement_UERJ_2011.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Filho-AdSQCDConfinement.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Some Milestones in the Study of Confinement
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Prospects+in+Theoretical+Physics+2023+--+Understanding+Confinement"} Prospects in Theoretical Physics 2023 – Understanding Confinement
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.ias.edu/video/some-milestones-study-confinement"} web
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/TvIz-6YOdKs"} YT
          %blockquote
            %p
              %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/TvIz-6YOdKs?t=2413"}> 40:13
              \: “Personally, I think
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FQCD"} this setup
              really implies that pure
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SU
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(N)
                gauge theory
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge-string+duality"} dual
              to a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
          %h3#in_mtheory_on_manifolds
            In M-theory on
            = succeed "-manifolds" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
          %p
            An idea for how to demonstrate confinement in models of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+G%E2%82%82-manifolds"} M-theory on G₂-manifolds
            is given in
          %ul
            %li#AtiyahWitten01
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                  \-Theory dynamics on a manifold of
                  = succeed "-holonomy" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi G
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0107177"} arXiv:hep-th/0107177
          %p based on
          %ul
            %li#AtiyahMaldacenaVafa00
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Juan+Maldacena"} Juan Maldacena
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
              = succeed "," do
                %em An M-theory Flop as a Large N Duality
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0011256"} arXiv:hep-th/0011256
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bobby+Acharya"}> Bobby Acharya
              ,
              %em
                Confining Strings from
                = succeed "-holonomy" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0101206"}> arXiv:hep-th/0101206
              )
          %p For review see
          %ul
            %li#AcharyaGukov04
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bobby+Acharya"}> Bobby Acharya
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergei+Gukov"} Sergei Gukov
              = succeed "," do
                %em M theory and Singularities of Exceptional Holonomy Manifolds
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0409191"} arXiv:hep-th/0409191
        .revisedby
